  \mathcal{I}$ such that $k < m$, the composition operation $\Pcomp^k$ birestricts to the set of
  $m$-cells $C_m$.
\end{corollary}

n34925.content:
\begin{construction}[Underlying single-sorted finite category]
  \label{def:SingleSortedNCategory_underlying}
  \uses{
    cor:SingleSorted_underlying_source_birestriction,
    cor:SingleSorted_underlying_target_birestriction,
    cor:SingleSorted_underlying_comp_birestriction
  }
  \lean{HigherCategoryTheory.SingleSorted.NCategory.underlying}
  \leanok
  Let $\mathsf{C}$ be a single-sorted $n$-category, and let $m \in \mathbb{N}$ with $m < n$. The
  \emph{underlying $m$-category} of $\mathsf{C}$ is the single-sorted $m$-category $\mathsf{C}^{<m}$
  defined on the set of $m$-cells $C_m$, with the source, target, and composition operations given
  by the birestrictions of those of $\mathsf{C}$ to $C_m$.
\end{construction}

